\title{islasso: The Induced Smoothed Lasso}
\description{
Estimation and inference for lasso and elastic-net regularised regression models through
the induced smoothing approach: the non-smooth penalty is replaced by its expectation under
the approximate sampling distribution of the estimator, so that standard errors (sandwich
formula) and Wald tests are available for all the coefficients.
}
\details{
Main functions: \code{\link[=islasso]{islasso()}} fits a model at a given value of the tuning parameter (chosen by
cross-validation if missing), \code{\link[=islasso.path]{islasso.path()}} fits a regularisation path, with
\code{\link[=GoF.islasso.path]{GoF.islasso.path()}} and \code{\link[=aic.islasso]{aic.islasso()}} selecting the tuning parameter by information
criteria; \code{\link[=relax.islasso]{relax.islasso()}} refits a relaxed model. Methods for \link[=summary.islasso]{summary()},
\link[=confint.islasso]{confint()}, \link[=anova.islasso]{anova()} (general linear hypotheses),
\link[=predict.islasso]{predict()} and \link[=plot.islasso]{plot()} are available.
}
